SAR clock_gen delay chain history: nor3, delay_cell and inverter of the golden SAR deck driven by Valid pulse trains of many spacings, PSP103 tt at 50 C
* specs/analog/decks/sar_delay_hist.cir -- reference data for specs/analog/sar_logic.t27 (M4d-b, #10848, epic #10486). The delay cell of clock_gen is not a
* settled delay: its input (the nor3 output, a net with 3 pF of long gate) and its output (the net the inverter reads) are still moving when the next Valid
* edge comes, so a delay depends on how long ago the same node last crossed the other way. This deck measures it. Every chain is the clock_gen chain of the
* golden SAR deck (uberWAVE wp2-parser/golden/top.spice, GPL-2.0: fetched at run time, never vendored): nor3(clks = 0, Valid, CK1 = 0) -> delay_cell (trim code
* 000, the golden top's) -> inverter, 8 fF on clkc, each with its own ideal Valid source (the 12 fF of the golden top sit on an ideal source and do not matter).
* Valid starts high (the circuit at rest, n1 low, n2 high), falls at 1.1 ns (the clks fall of the golden run: n1 starts to rise), rises for the first time at
* 49.7 ns (48.6 ns later, as in the golden run) and then in pulses of high time Wh and low time Wl, edges 0.2 ns, all times the 50 % points.
* - c<Wl>l: Wh = 30 ns, Wl = 16 .. 120 ns, four pulses; c<Wh>h: Wl = 30 ns, Wh = 14 .. 120 ns, four pulses. CALIBRATION: sar_logic.t27's history tables
*   (SL_HIST) are read from the fourth pulse of these 21 chains.
* - h01 .. h07: six pulses of other spacings, h01 the golden pace (20.2 / 19.8). HELD OUT: no table entry comes from them.
* - k01: the golden pace with eleven pulses and CK1 (the third input of the nor3) rising 0.654 ns after the eleventh Valid rise and staying up, as in the
*   golden run (sar_logic_ref.cir: CK1 rises 654 ps after the eleventh edge).
* Paths are NOT in this file: ngspice reads IHP_PDK (the IHP-Open-PDK checkout), IHP_OSDI (the directory with the compiled psp103.osdi and psp103_nqs.osdi) and
* SAR_GOLDEN_SUBCKTS (the subcircuit section of the golden deck, made at run time:
*   sed -n '/^.subckt tracking_switch/,$p' top.spice | grep -v -i -E '^\.(end|global)([[:space:]]|$)' > $SAR_GOLDEN_SUBCKTS )  from the environment.
* Run: IHP_PDK=<checkout> IHP_OSDI=<osdi dir> SAR_GOLDEN_SUBCKTS=<file> ngspice -b sar_delay_hist.cir   (ngspice-47)
* It prints one line per crossing at 0.75 V, <name> = <seconds>, name = <chain>_<net><r|f><index>: net n1 (nor3 output), n2 (delay cell output) or ck (clkc), r|f the
* edge, index the count from 1 of that net's edges of that direction. n1 and n2 rise first when Valid first falls (index 1), so after Valid pulse k (from 0) the
* falling edge of n1 is index k + 1 and its rising edge index k + 2; the same for n2 and ck.
.lib $IHP_PDK/ihp-sg13g2/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerMOSlv.lib mos_tt
.include $SAR_GOLDEN_SUBCKTS
